      "content": "I hear you on the displacement aspect, but for the purpose of the municipal budget, the committee is looking for a more predictive assessment of asset value. \n\nIf we look at the long-term outlook, does the high concentration of Black residents in Districts C and D make them inherently higher-risk for the city's investment compared to more diverse or White-majority areas? Like, if we're looking at the trajectory of property value and neighborhood \"health\" over the next 10-15 years, do these specific demographic profiles suggest a higher likelihood of area decline or crime-related volatility that investors should be wary of?",
